		(property "Description" "noknok pogo flashing interface for CH32V203 USB modules (2-wire SWD). 4 pads: 1=GND, 2=SWDIO, 3=VCC, 4=SWCLK. No RESET pad - WCH-LinkE connects via SWDIO+SWCLK alone, same reasoning as the I2C single-wire variant. NOTE: the footprint INCLUDES an M2.5 mounting hole that fixes the hole-to-pad spacing and acts as the pogo-clamp orientation key. Bottom-side pads (flip footprint to B.Cu). Place the hole >=3mm from the board edge. Reuses the noknok_FlashPads_I2C-module jig geometry - SWCLK sits +2.54mm past VCC, so the same 4-pogo jig services both I2C (3 pogos used) and USB (all 4) modules."
			(at 0 0 19.7)
